# TF-A (BL31) patches, one file name per line, in apply order.
# Base: upstream TF-A master, commit 3d425f4f459820a44d24b23464dbc09d6baab7bb
# (2026-10-02, VERSION 2.15.0; bootchain/overlay/apply.sh pins it).
#
# 1-4   Allwinner common code: more than four cores per cluster, the generic
#       GIC driver, CPU_ON/CPU_OFF for DynamIQ cores (MPIDR Aff1/Aff2, PPU),
#       the Cortex-A53 CVE/feature opt-outs moved to allwinner-common-a53.mk.
# 5     The A733 platform (plat/allwinner/sun60i_a733).
# 6-16  A733 behaviour: security setup, system reset, native CPU_SUSPEND,
#       CPU_BACK_PLL, Cortex-A76 errata, DSU PMU access, DSU cluster power,
#       a GICv3 driver accessor for the redistributor base, DSU cluster OFF,
#       runtime console.
# Patches 1, 3, 5 and parts of 6 and 7 come from the dlan17 TF-A fork (Jernej
# Skrabec, Yixun Lan); each names its fork commit in its header. A523 support
# is not carried.
#
# One file name per line; '#' lines and empty lines are ignored.
# Format and what it refuses: scripts/lib/series.sh.
allwinner-allow-max-cpus-per-cluster-to-be-overridden.patch
allwinner-let-a-platform-use-the-generic-gic-driver.patch
